  "result": "Perfect! Payment terms have been successfully implemented. Here's what was added:\n\n**Changes Made:**\n\n1. **Error Code** (`src/errors.js`): Added `TERMS_INVALID` error for invalid payment terms.\n\n2. **Invoice Creation** (`src/invoices.js`):\n   - Updated `createInvoice` to accept optional `terms` parameter (defaults to `'NET30'`)\n   - Added `validateTerms()` helper that accepts `'NET14'`, `'NET30'`, or `'EOM'`\n   - Added `calculateDueDate()` helper that computes:\n     - **NET14**: issue date + 14 days\n     - **NET30**: issue date + 30 days\n     - **EOM**: last day of the month\n   - Both `terms` and `dueDate` are now set on returned invoices\n\n3. **Tests** (`test/invoices.test.js`): Added 13 comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Default NET30 terms\n   - All three term types (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n   - Edge cases: end-of-month, leap years, December to next year\n   - Month/year boundary crossings\n   - Invalid terms error handling\n\nAll 181 tests pass (168 original + 13 new).",
